# Netlify redirects — adlerrochefort.com
#
# Rules declared in netlify.toml are evaluated before this file. The paths here
# do not overlap with any of them, so ordering is not load-bearing; this file
# holds every 301 created by the blog consolidation and the service-URL
# standardisation.
#
# Each retired path is listed twice: the bare form, and a splat that covers the
# trailing slash plus anything ever linked below it. Query strings are carried
# over by Netlify automatically.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Blog consolidation, August 2026.
#
# Two Portuguese articles competed with a stronger article on the same query
# and split the ranking signal. Their unique sections were folded into the
# surviving article; the retired URLs point at it permanently. Both carry
# status: merged in data/articles.json, so no listing, sitemap or feed can
# reintroduce them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/blog/seguro-individual-automovel        /blog/seguro-automovel-guia-completo/   301!
/blog/seguro-individual-automovel/*      /blog/seguro-automovel-guia-completo/   301!

/blog/seguro-habitacao-proteger-casa     /blog/multirriscos-habitacao/           301!
/blog/seguro-habitacao-proteger-casa/*   /blog/multirriscos-habitacao/           301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service URL standardisation, August 2026.
#
# Three URL patterns coexisted for commercial pages. Everything now lives under
# /seguros/{slug}/. Both retired paths carry organic history — the condominium
# page in particular — so these redirects are permanent and must not be
# removed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/seguro-auto                             /seguros/auto/                          301!
/seguro-auto/*                           /seguros/auto/                          301!

/seguros-condominios-algarve             /seguros/condominios/                   301!
/seguros-condominios-algarve/*           /seguros/condominios/                   301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Path-segment truncation.
#
# /en/insurance/tvde/ is the only page under /en/insurance/, so a visitor who
# trims the last segment — a habit URLs invite — lands on nothing. Portuguese
# has a real hub at /seguros/; English does not, so the parent points at the
# English home page rather than 404.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/en/insurance                            /en/                                    301
/en/insurance/                           /en/                                    301

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Moved here from netlify.toml, August 2026.
#
# Every permanent redirect on the site is now declared in this one file, so a
# retired URL can be traced without reading two configurations. The short links
# under /go/ stay in netlify.toml: they are 302s used for campaign tracking,
# not part of the URL history.
#
# The EN contact path has never been a page — the English contact form lives in
# a section of the English home page.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/en/contact                              /en/#contact                            301!
/en/contact/                             /en/#contact                            301!

